# Persistence & sync rules

- Dexie is the source of truth. Read the schema in `lib/db/dexie.ts` before adding
  a table; migrations are additive and need an `.upgrade()` backfill.
- Write path: `TransactionContext.runInTransaction([...tables], async (ctx) => { ... })`
  → `ctx.table<T>("name").put(row)` → `append(entityType, op, row, { tx: ctx, baseUpdatedAt })`.
  Never call `db.outboxMutations.add(...)` directly.
- Local-only tables (`tripBudgets`, `packingItems`, `currencyRates`, `transitSegments`,
  `journalDayEntries`, `dailyStepCounts`, `tripPins`, `feedItems`, `travelDocuments`,
  `polls`, `pollVotes`, `profiles`, `stagedTripMedia`) must not append outbox entries.
- New synced entity requires: Dexie table + Supabase migration + RLS + mapper in
  `lib/supabase/mappers.ts` + `SYNC_TABLE_DEFINITIONS` in `lib/sync/cloud-sync.ts` +
  `OutboxEntityType` in `lib/sync/types.ts`.
- Money fields are `bigint` minor units; validate with `features/domain/money.ts`.
- BigInt is not JSON-serializable — outbox payloads are structured-cloned only.
- `watch*` repository methods return a disposer; hooks must unsubscribe.
- Invitation accept/reject is remote-first (`accept_trip_invitation` RPC) — document
  any other remote-first exception in `memory/MEMORY.md`.
